# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Optimize for target hardware {#2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"
msgstr ""
"2. I-optimize para sa target na hardware {#2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we have created the circuits, we can optimize them for a target "
"hardware. We pick a utility scale QPU.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayong nalikha na natin ang mga circuit, maaari na nating i-optimize ang "
"mga ito para sa isang target na hardware. Pumipili tayo ng utility scale "
"QPU.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, we transpile the circuits to the target backend using a preset pass "
"manager.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, tina-transpile natin ang mga circuit sa target backend gamit ang "
"isang preset pass manager.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Execute on target hardware {#3-execute-on-target-hardware}"
msgstr "3. Isagawa sa target na hardware {#3-execute-on-target-hardware}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After optimizing the circuits for hardware execution, we are ready to run "
"them on the target hardware and collect samples for ground state energy "
"estimation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos i-optimize ang mga circuit para sa hardware execution, handa na "
"tayong patakbuhin ang mga ito sa target na hardware at mangolekta ng mga "
"sample para sa ground state energy estimation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. Post-process results {#4-post-process-results}"
msgstr "4. Post-process ng mga resulta {#4-post-process-results}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we aggregate the counts for increasing Krylov dimensions in a "
"cumulative fashion. Using the cumulative counts, we will span subspaces for "
"increasing Krylov dimension and analyze the convergence behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, pino-pool natin ang mga count para sa dumaraming Krylov dimension "
"sa cumulative na paraan. Gamit ang mga cumulative count, magsa-span tayo ng "
"mga subspace para sa dumaraming Krylov dimension at susuriin ang behavior ng"
" convergence.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To project and diagonalize the Hamiltonian, we use capabilities from "
"[`qiskit-addon-sqd`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-sqd/). The addon "
"offers functionalities to project Pauli string-based Hamiltonians onto a "
"subspace and solves for eigenvalues using `SciPy`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para i-project at i-diagonalize ang Hamiltonian, gumagamit tayo ng mga "
"kakayahan mula sa [`qiskit-addon-sqd`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-"
"addon-sqd/). Nag-aalok ang addon ng mga functionality para i-project ang mga"
" Pauli string-based na Hamiltonian sa isang subspace at naglulutas ng mga "
"eigenvalue gamit ang `SciPy`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In principle, we can filter out bitstrings with incorrect pattern before "
"spanning the subspace. For example, the ground state for the "
"antiferromagnetic Hamiltonian in this lesson typically has an equal number "
"of \"up\" and \"down\" spins, that is, the number of \"1\"s in the bitstring"
" should be exactly half the total number of bits (spins) in the system. The "
"following function filters out bitstrings with incorrect number of \"1\"s "
"from the counts.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa prinsipyo, maaari tayong mag-filter ng mga bitstring na may maling "
"pattern bago mag-span ng subspace. Halimbawa, ang ground state para sa "
"antiferromagnetic Hamiltonian sa araling ito ay karaniwang may pantay na "
"bilang ng \"up\" at \"down\" na spin, ibig sabihin, ang bilang ng \"1\" sa "
"bitstring ay dapat na eksaktong kalahati ng kabuuang bilang ng bit (spin) sa"
" sistema. Ang sumusunod na function ay nagfi-filter ng mga bitstring na may "
"maling bilang ng \"1\" mula sa mga count.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using bitstrings with the correct number of up/down electrons, we span "
"subspaces and compute eigenvalues for increasing Krylov dimension. Depending"
" on the problem size and available classical resources, we may need to adopt"
" subsampling (similar to the [lesson on SQD](/learning/courses/quantum-"
"diagonalization-algorithms/sqd-implementation)) to keep the subspace "
"dimension in check. Moreover, we can apply the notion of configuration "
"recovery similar to Lesson 4. We can compute the electron occupancy per site"
" from reconstructed eigenstates and use the information to correct "
"bitstrings with an incorrect number of up/down electrons. We leave this as "
"an exercise for interested readers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamit ang mga bitstring na may tamang bilang ng up/down electron, nagsa-span"
" tayo ng mga subspace at kinokomputa ang mga eigenvalue para sa dumaraming "
"Krylov dimension. Depende sa laki ng problema at sa mga available na "
"klasikal na resources, maaaring kailanganin nating gumamit ng subsampling "
"(katulad ng [aralin sa SQD](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/sqd-implementation)) upang mapanatiling kontrolado ang dimensyon "
"ng subspace. Bukod pa rito, maaari tayong mag-apply ng konsepto ng "
"configuration recovery na katulad ng Aralin 4. Maaari tayong makalkula ang "
"electron occupancy bawat site mula sa mga nire-reconstruct na eigenstate at "
"gamitin ang impormasyong ito upang itama ang mga bitstring na may maling "
"bilang ng up/down electron. Iniiwan namin ito bilang ehersisyo para sa mga "
"interesadong mambabasa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we plot computed energy as a function of Krylov dimension and compare "
"with exact energy. The exact energy is computed separately using a classical"
" Brute force method. We can see that the estimated ground state energy "
"converges with increasing Krylov space dimension. Although Krylov dimension "
"of $5$ is limiting, the results still show impressive convergence, which is "
"expected to improve with a larger Krylov dimension [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, nipo-plot natin ang kinomputang enerhiya bilang function ng Krylov "
"dimension at ikukumpara sa eksaktong enerhiya. Ang eksaktong enerhiya ay "
"kinokomputa nang hiwalay gamit ang isang klasikal na Brute force method. "
"Makikita natin na ang tinatantyang ground state energy ay nako-converge sa "
"dumaraming dimensyon ng Krylov space. Bagaman ang Krylov dimension na $5$ ay"
" may limitasyon, ang mga resulta ay nagpapakita pa rin ng kahanga-hangang "
"convergence, na inaasahang mapabuti pa sa mas malaking Krylov dimension "
"[\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
